eir physical characteristics with their gender identity. Furthermore, estrogens influence the regulation of gonadotropin secretion, including hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone) and LH (luteinizing hormone). They also have an impact on prolactin levels and are associated with conditions like hyperprolactinemia. Overall, estrogens are vital for various physiological processes and health outcomes.\",5\r\n3631,PUBERTAD PRECOZ,\"La pubertad precoz es un desarrollo sexual anormalmente temprano en niños, caracterizado por la aparición de características sexuales secundarias antes de la edad normal, que se establece como antes de los 9 años para los niños y antes de los 7 años para las niñas. Esta condición puede ser clasificada como central o periférica y puede estar asociada a diversas condiciones médicas. Aunque no es la causa más frecuente, la pubertad precoz puede manifestarse como un síntoma relacionado con tumores de la glándula pineal. En resumen, la pubertad precoz es una manifestación clínica que conlleva importantes implicaciones médicas y requiere atención adecuada.\",10\r\n3638,GÓNADAS,\"GÓNADAS are the organs responsible for producing gametes, which are the reproductive cells necessary for sexual reproduction. In humans, the gonads are represented by the testes in males and the ovaries in females. Additionally, in the context of hormone therapy, gonads may undergo surgical alteration or removal, impacting their function in gamete production.\",6\r\n5273,PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL,\"Central precocious puberty, known in Spanish as \"\"pubertad precoz central,\"\" is a condition characterized by the early activation of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis. This condition leads to the development of secondary sexual characteristics before the age of 8 in girls and before the age of 9 in boys. The early onset of puberty in this manner signifies a significant deviation from the typical developmental timeline, prompting further medical evaluation and